---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import SeoNav from '../../components/SeoNav.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Clean metadata"
	lede="Every tag present, every value inside the limits each network truncates at."
	seo={{
		// Kept under 160 characters, which is where Google truncates. A longer
		// one would make this page report a warning and stop being the clean case.
		description:
			'Complete head metadata: an absolute 1200x630 og:image with declared dimensions and alt text, a matching canonical link, and a large summary card.',
		image: '/og/card.png',
		imageAlt: 'Abstract share card for the astro-ai example',
		imageSize: [1200, 630],
	}}
>
	<SeoNav />

	<Callout title="What to try" tone="accent">
		Open the share preview. The Issues tab says there is nothing to fix, and
		every card renders the wide image, because <code>twitter:card</code> is
		<code>summary_large_image</code> and the image is large enough for it.
	</Callout>

	<section class="panel" aria-label="Tags this page declares">
		<h2>What makes it clean</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><code>og:image</code> is an absolute URL, so a crawler can fetch it.</li>
			<li>It is 1200×630, the size the wide card is designed around.</li>
			<li>
				<code>og:image:width</code> and <code>og:image:height</code> are
				declared, so the first share renders with the image instead of waiting
				for a crawler to measure it.
			</li>
			<li><code>og:image:alt</code> is set, so the card is readable on a screen reader.</li>
			<li><code>og:url</code> and the canonical link agree.</li>
			<li>The title is under 60 characters and the description under 160.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<Callout title="Compare the cards">
		Even with identical tags the eight cards differ: LinkedIn drops the
		description, Google shows a breadcrumb instead of a domain, WhatsApp puts
		the image in a small square, and X only shows the wide banner because
		<code>twitter:card</code> asks for it.
	</Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
	.panel {
		border: 1px solid #14805e;
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
	}

	ul {
		color: #aeb6c5;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.1rem;
	}

	code {
		color: #86efac;
	}
</style>
